## What one more room costs

The step from a two-room to a three-room flat is not the same everywhere. It is largest in {cdStepDear}, where a three-room costs {cdStepDearPctEn}% more than a two-room, and smallest in {cdStepCheap} at {cdStepCheapPctEn}%. In Bratislava it is {cdStepBaEn}%.

For a buyer that is practical information: in one town an extra room means half the price of the flat again, in another an eighth. The per-square-metre view shows why. In {cdM2Down} of the {cdM2Total} towns a larger flat is cheaper per metre — space costs less the more of it you buy. The exceptions are {cdM2Up}, where it works the other way.

